<h1 class="article-title">Made in Liepāja Youth Ideas Workshop and Competition Concludes</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>The “Made in Liepāja” youth ideas workshop, organised by the Liepāja SEZ Authority, concluded with an animated discussion and a business lunch. All general-school students were invited to contribute to shaping the business environment. In cooperation with the Education Authority and the city’s schools, a competition sought young people’s ideas for developing Liepāja’s economy. In total, 39 submissions were received, from individual students and groups.</p><p>Liepāja SEZ CEO Uldis Hmieļevskis emphasises that young people are the driving force behind the city’s future: their knowledge, creativity and initiative will be crucial to Liepāja’s development. It is therefore important to involve them early in discussions about business, the fundamentals of economic growth and industry prospects. “This certainly helps young people better understand their interests, recognise future opportunities and choose suitable careers. It also gives them insight into industrial trends and the city’s economic goals. Educated, enterprising and determined young people form a strong foundation for Liepāja’s growth,” he says. He was particularly pleased by the students’ conclusions and proposals, which demonstrated analytical and strategic thinking as well as a genuine desire to help shape the city’s future.</p><p>A specially appointed jury of representatives from the Education Authority, Liepāja SEZ Authority and local businesses evaluated submissions from schools and Liepāja State Technical School. After lengthy discussions, the jury selected five entries for encouragement prizes — Liepāja gift cards — and five award-winning entries. Their authors took part in a discussion and business lunch with Uldis Hmieļevskis. Afterwards, the young participants said it was valuable to discuss entrepreneurship and decision-making and learn how Liepāja’s business environment is formed, including less visible challenges faced by businesses.</p><p>The workshop and competition took place as part of the “Made in Liepāja” exhibition. Participants selected one of the proposed topics, conducted research at the exhibition by interviewing business owners and company representatives, and prepared conclusions and recommendations. The Liepāja SEZ Authority thanks all the active students and their teachers. When the weather becomes warmer, all participants will also be invited on a tour to see Liepāja’s economic environment and activities in the SEZ first-hand.</p><p>Award winners:</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Magdalēne Maija Valtere</li></ul><p>Topic: Where does money come from?</p><ul><li>Liepāja State Gymnasium — Elīza Bauseniece</li></ul><p>Topic: Five essential features that make Liepāja a high-quality business environment.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Jeļizaveta Kovaļova, Viktorija Siļčonoka</li></ul><p>Topic: Five risks that could negatively affect business.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Krista Jonika and Maija Alise Zvirbule</li></ul><p>Topic: Five most important factors that make a company attractive to employees.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Paula Roliča and Līva Vēkause</li></ul><p>Topic: Five most important factors that make a company attractive to employees.</p><p>Encouragement prizes:</p><ul><li>Liepāja Liedaga Secondary School — Sofija Bičāne, Ļevs Celoguzs, Ariadna Hromovskiha, Viktorija Jegorova, Artjoms Jonkins, Marats Kerimovs, Poļina Pavļučenko, Staņislavs Škrobs, Kirils Volkovs, Vladislavs Žerebcovs.</li></ul><p>Topic: Five risks that could negatively affect business.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Kārlis Ļaudobelis, Marks Zveja, Dēvids Einas.</li></ul><p>Topic: Five risks that could negatively affect business.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Nikija Mikāle.</li></ul><p>Topic: Five risks that could negatively affect business.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Draudzīgā aicinājuma Secondary School — Sanija Mače</li></ul><p>Topic: Five most important factors that make a company attractive to employees.</p><ul><li>Liepāja Liedaga Secondary School — Alise Kalašņikova</li></ul><p>Topic: Where does money come from?</p></div>
